 1, which is presumably how the error survived. The sign argument built on it (\"the -2 subtracts the symmetric and alternating eigenvalues already counted\") therefore has no support, and h > 0 at q_0 > 1 so it does not deliver a negative sign either. (2) ACCURACY FRAMING / CALIBRATION PASS-THROUGH: the quoted percentages are errors on the TOTAL ATOMIC MASS, of which the binding energy (the part the framework supplies) is under 1 percent: B/M = 0.694% for Be-9 and 0.824% for C-12. Converting: Be-9 0.192% to 0.108% of mass is 16.10 to 9.05 MeV, i.e. 27.7% to 15.6% of its 58.17 MeV binding; C-12 0.081% to 0.002% is 9.05 to 0.22 MeV, i.e. 9.8% to 0.24% of its 92.16 MeV binding. A \"0.072% mean\" headline is roughly 120x smaller than the corresponding error on the framework-supplied quantity. (3) Under the absolute-mass excision (AGENTS.md, 2026-08-11) an atomic mass in MeV is not a framework prediction, so these should be restated as binding-energy accuracy. (4) tr_M is written here as sum_lambda w_lambda tr_lambda / dim_lambda, colliding with the y_lambda family used by sibling blocks (notation register warns y/w/tilde-w are distinct at q != 1). (5) Arithmetic that DOES check: abs(beta_4) times alpha = 0.083 x 3.74 = 0.3104 MeV.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:w01","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:w01","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:w01","notes":"FIXED inline: \"(with dramatic per-atom improvements: ...)\" -> \"(per-atom improvements: ...)\". One word, pure prose, numbers untouched. $$ delimiters re-verified balanced.","hi